 "entries": [
  {
   "date": "2026-06-12",
   "title": "Coffee Crop Update – Grounds for Caution",
   "url": "https://www.sucdenfinancial.com/en/market-insights/soft-commodities-outlook/coffee-market-outlook/coffee-crop-update-grounds-for-caution/",
   "key_points": [
    "Brazil 2026/27 raised to 76–77m bags (from 72–73m), conilon ~25m; good-cup prices near BRL 1,700 keep growers slow sellers, so the crop reaches the market gradually.",
    "2025/26 Brazil exports ~38.2m bags, below the 3- and 6-year averages; carryover ~4.8m at end-June 2026, possibly ~17.8m a year later if exports recover to ~43m.",
    "World 2025/26 still tight (production ~172m vs use ~176m); demand growth led by Asia and a shift toward robusta in blends.",
    "Arb expected to keep narrowing toward 70–80¢ if robusta demand holds and Brazil arabica flows freely.",
    "Risks: El Niño for Vietnam/Indonesia and Brazil's Aug–Oct flowering, fertiliser costs (urea ~+50%), freight and energy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-01-23",
   "title": "Coffee Crop Update – Walking a Fine Line",
   "url": "https://www.sucdenfinancial.com/en/market-insights/soft-commodities-outlook/coffee-market-outlook/coffee-crop-update-walking-a-fine-line/",
   "key_points": [
    "Brazil 2025/26 held at 64m bags (39 arabica / 25 conilon) with only ~1m bags carried into 2026/27.",
    "First 2026/27 Brazil view ~72.5m bags (47.5 arabica): would turn a ~3.2m-bag world deficit (2025/26, 176m demand) into a ~5m surplus.",
    "Vietnam ~29m bags with ~10m sold early; Ethiopia shipping ~7.3m bags a year, output possibly ~11m.",
    "Roasters' modest commercial length suggests they are not extending cover at current flat prices."
   ]
  }
 ]
}